# drop-LESS conversion: gate reports.
*-gate.json

# `baseline/` USED TO BE IGNORED HERE. It is now TRACKED, deliberately and TEMPORARILY,
# for the duration of the drop-LESS conversion — untrack it again at P8 (see S47).
#
# WHY: every 4th-layer verification round is required to prove it did not touch `baseline/`,
# and the proof it was told to use is `git status --porcelain`. While the directory was
# ignored, that command could not go red no matter what happened to the reference build —
# the single most important invariant in the plan was being reported green by a check
# structurally incapable of failing (found 2026-08-07, recorded as S45).
# `doc/baseline-manifest.sha256` pins the bytes, but nothing made a WRITE visible at a glance.
# Tracking it makes any write show up in `git status` and `git diff` immediately.
#
# COST: ~832 KB / 86 files of build output in history, and `npm run baseline` now produces a
# working-tree diff instead of nothing. That is the point — it should be loud.